# Merge behaviour by file TYPE - the mechanical half of the conflict ladder (CLAUDE.md).
# Everything git can resolve without judgement is resolved here, so an agent only ever sees a
# conflict that genuinely needs a decision.

# The desk ledgers are append-only event logs: two hands appending at EOF are BOTH right, and a
# plain rebase would conflict on every concurrent append. Union keeps both rows. Safe because
# every reader of a .jsonl here is order-insensitive - `data/runs.jsonl` is keyed by run id,
# `data/snapshots.jsonl` by (ts, subject, field), the read-ledger takes the newest row per path -
# so a union merge can add a duplicate but can never produce a wrong answer. A duplicate run id
# is a visible defect; a silently dropped run is not.
*.jsonl merge=union

# Scripts are POSIX and are run by bash on Windows machines too: a CRLF checkout breaks the
# shebang line. Windows defaults to autocrlf=true, which would otherwise mangle them.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf

# Everything an agent reads or writes is LF, on every machine. Mixed endings turn a one-word
# edit into a whole-file diff, and a whole-file diff cannot be reviewed.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# Rendered and captured artifacts get NO driver on purpose. A collision must surface as a real
# conflict and go to the owner - a chart or a screenshot is nobody's to overwrite.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.parquet binary
*.ipynb  -diff
fund text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
